
# Dataset preparation

## Source

The project uses the external **Mpox Skin Lesion Dataset Version 2.0 (MSLD v2.0)**. Obtain it from its official Kaggle dataset page:

https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/joydippaul/mpox-skin-lesion-dataset-version-20-msld-v20

Follow Kaggle's current access and usage terms. Do not upload the dataset images to this repository unless you have explicit redistribution permission.

## Expected organization

The final experiment's exact folder names must match the scripts and split manifests. A common prepared layout is:

```text
FINAL_PIPELINE_DATASET/
├── Train/
│   ├── CHP/
│   ├── CWP/
│   ├── HEALTHY/
│   ├── HFMD/
│   ├── MSL/
│   └── MKP/
├── Val/
│   └── [same six class folders]
└── Test/
    └── [same six class folders]
```

If your experiment uses `Valid` rather than `Val`, update the configuration and all scripts consistently. Do not silently rename folders if a notebook or split-generation script relies on the original names.

## Data leakage precautions

- Keep the independent test set isolated from model development.
- Fit preprocessing parameters only on the training data where applicable.
- Apply augmentation only to training samples.
- Preserve the original split/fold assignments.
- Save a manifest of file paths and labels for every split.
- Run duplicate screening across Train, Val, and Test before training.

## Class labels

CHP: Chickenpox; CWP: Cowpox; HEALTHY: Healthy; HFMD: Hand-foot-mouth disease; MSL: Measles; MKP: Monkeypox.

The mapping in this document is descriptive. Use the exact numeric class-index mapping from the released experiment code.
